component SigilLanguage {
  goal {
    Define the versioned source and interpretation contract for Sigil documents.

    Give deterministic tools one structural model for components, expansions, sections, concepts, imports, and recoverable diagnostics.
  }

  interface {
    LanguageVersion {
      sigilVersion = "0.5.0"

      workspace configuration declares the LanguageVersion that governs interpretation
    }

    SourceDocument {
      accepts UTF-8 .sigil source containing imports, components, expands, sections, concept blocks, and semantic lines

      preserves recovered declarations, semantic lines, concept identities, and source ranges

      reports structural diagnostics while retaining a partial document when practical
    }

    ComponentContract {
      component defines the reusable public contract of one coherent system part through its goal and interface

      expand contributes collective operational detail without changing or overriding the public contract

      goal publicly states the component's responsibility, boundary, and intended outcome

      interface exposes the operations, data, events, results, failures, and observable promises available to dependents
    }

    ConceptIdentity {
      a concept block groups one or more related semantic lines under a reusable identifier

      a concept is public when it occurs in interface and otherwise remains private to its component and matching expands

      a component and all matching expands share one flat concept namespace

      repeated blocks with the same resolved identifier contribute collectively without overriding one another

      imported public concepts retain their originating identity when reused contextually
    }

    ImportSemantics {
      import is the sole declaration of dependency on another Sigil component

      a named import exposes the imported component's public goal, interface, and public concept identities

      imported operational detail and private concepts remain unavailable to dependents
    }

    SectionSemantics {
      state describes meaningful configurations, modes, and domain conditions that exist or change during execution

      logic describes behavior, flows, algorithms, transformations, decisions, and lifecycle transitions

      constraints describe rules, policies, invariants, architecture decisions, and binding technology choices

      decisions describes the durable rationale for a chosen course, including context, scope, assumptions, trade-offs, design issues addressed, discarded alternatives, consequences, and revisit conditions

      cases describe representative outcomes, examples, edge cases, and observable acceptance scenarios
    }

    SemanticLineDiscipline {
      each non-empty semantic line expresses one distinct idea

      blank lines separate distinct prose-level ideas for readability and do not create semantic units
    }
  }
}

expand SigilLanguage {
  constraints {
    LanguageVersion {
      LanguageVersion is the sole owner of the Sigil language and workspace-configuration version literal.

      Tools reject configured language versions they do not support.

      During pre-production 0.y.z development, breaking interpretation changes increment the minor version and reset the patch version.

      After 1.0.0, breaking interpretation changes require a new major version.

      Compatible additions and clarifications use the appropriate semantic version increment.
    }

    SourceDocument {
      Every component contains goal and interface sections.

      Ungrouped interface content remains parseable and produces one warning for each contiguous ungrouped region.

      Invalid structure produces source-ranged diagnostics while recoverable content remains available.
    }

    ComponentContract {
      Component dependencies are declared through imports and are not repeated as interface dependency lines.

      Matching expands add detail collectively and never override the component declaration or another expand.

      A dependent receives the imported component's public contract without its state, logic, constraints, decisions, cases, or private concepts.

      Implementation-hiding rules belong in constraints unless they define an observable promise.
    }

    ConceptIdentity {
      Concept blocks are flat and cannot nest.

      Every concept block contains at least one semantic line.

      Concept identifiers match [A-Za-z][A-Za-z0-9_-]* and contain no spaces.

      PascalCase without hyphens or underscores is preferred but not required for validity.

      Concept references are case-sensitive.

      Accessible identifiers are unique without regard to case across the transitive import graph.

      Sigil provides no dotted concept notation, qualification, aliases, or local shadowing.

      Reusing an imported concept preserves its originating identity while keeping importer semantic lines contextual to the importer.

      Reusing an imported concept in interface re-exposes the same identity to downstream importers.

      Provider context never includes semantic lines contributed by consumers.

      A whole-word accessible identifier in semantic content resolves as a reference.

      Unmatched words remain ordinary semantic content without unresolved-concept diagnostics.

      Concept identities provide grouping, reuse, navigation, and highlighting but define no source-anchor behavior.
    }

    ImportSemantics {
      Ordinary file imports resolve against the named .sigil source.

      Directory imports resolve through ModuleIndexFile.

      Imported names must resolve to components exposed by the selected source or directory-import surface.

      Import cycles and unresolved paths or names produce diagnostics with partial resolution when practical.
    }

    SectionSemantics {
      decisions is an optional expand section.

      decisions content is free-form and does not require concept blocks, labeled fields, or a complete rationale schema.

      decisions records concise conclusions and supporting rationale rather than prompts, session transcripts, or hidden reasoning.

      When present, decision scope states the boundary where a chosen course applies and its important exclusions without attempting to enumerate every current dependent.

      A binding outcome remains in constraints; decisions explains why that outcome was selected.
    }

    SemanticLineDiscipline {
      Distinct prose-level ideas are separated by blank lines in every section.

      Lines in one compact free-form construct may remain adjacent when separation would reduce readability.
    }
  }

  cases {
    LanguageVersion {
      A tool that does not support the configured LanguageVersion reports an error before interpreting workspace Sigil files.

      A document configured for an earlier incompatible version is not silently reinterpreted using 0.5.0 semantics.
    }

    SourceDocument {
      A malformed but recoverable component retains its declarations and semantic lines with source-ranged diagnostics.

      A contiguous ungrouped interface region produces one SIGIL_MISSING_CONCEPT_IDENTIFIER warning.

      An empty or nested concept block is invalid.
    }

    ComponentContract {
      A component can be understood through its goal and interface without reading its expands or implementation.

      Multiple matching expands remain separately sourced contributions to one collected operational description.
    }

    ConceptIdentity {
      Reusing one public concept in interface, state, logic, constraints, decisions, or cases preserves one collective identity.

      Importing two different public concepts whose identifiers compare equal without regard to case produces an ambiguous-concept diagnostic.

      A concept introduced only outside interface remains private.

      An importer's contextual occurrence appears in importer context without changing provider context.
    }

    ImportSemantics {
      Importing Name makes Name's public contract available without exposing its collected expansions.

      A missing source, component, or directory-import name produces a stable diagnostic and partial resolution when practical.
    }

    SectionSemantics {
      An expand may omit decisions without losing validity.

      A decisions section may contain free prose or named concept blocks with rationale labels.

      A binding stack choice appears in constraints while a corresponding decisions entry explains its alternatives and trade-offs.
    }
  }
}

component SigilWorkspaceConfig {
  goal {
    Define the configuration contract that selects and identifies one Sigil workspace.

    Keep workspace boundaries and source discovery independent from package manifests and directory-import indexes.
  }

  interface {
    ConfigFile {
      filename: .sigil/config.json

      location: workspace root
    }

    ConfiguredLanguageVersion {
      sigilVersion: the supported Sigil language version used to interpret the workspace
    }

    WorkspaceBoundary {
      workspace.name: non-empty stable workspace identifier

      workspace.members: optional array of unique workspace-relative project-root paths
    }

    SourceSelection {
      files.include: non-empty array of workspace-relative POSIX glob strings

      files.exclude?: array of workspace-relative POSIX glob strings
    }

    ToolConfiguration {
      tools?: object of namespaced JSON objects preserved for host integrations
    }
  }
}

expand SigilWorkspaceConfig {
  constraints {
    ConfigFile {
      ConfigFile is the sole authority for the Sigil workspace boundary.

      The directory containing ConfigFile is the workspace root and root project location.
    }

    ConfiguredLanguageVersion {
      The configured sigilVersion must equal a language version supported by the interpreting tool.
    }

    WorkspaceBoundary {
      Each workspace.members entry declares one additional project root in the same workspace.

      Member paths are unique, non-root, workspace-relative directories that cannot escape the workspace or overlap.

      A declared member does not contain its own ConfigFile.

      A nested directory with its own ConfigFile is an independent workspace and must be excluded from every configured parent.

      Package and repository workspace manifests do not declare Sigil workspace members.
    }

    SourceSelection {
      SourceSelection controls source discovery but does not declare workspace members or restrict ModuleIndexFile locations.
    }

    ModuleIndexFile {
      ModuleIndexFile has no workspace-discovery or membership authority.
    }
  }
}

component SigilModuleIndex {
  goal {
    Define the explicit directory-import index for an included Sigil directory.

    Provide intentional directory-import shorthand without changing component visibility or workspace discovery.
  }

  interface {
    ModuleIndexFile {
      filename: #module.sigil

      location: any included directory in a Sigil workspace
    }

    DirectoryImportSurface {
      a directory import @path resolves through @path/#module.sigil

      includes components declared directly in ModuleIndexFile

      includes components named by direct imports in ModuleIndexFile
    }

    ComponentVisibility {
      every component remains importable through its explicit .sigil source path regardless of ModuleIndexFile
    }

    ModuleIndexContents {
      contains at least one local component declaration

      may additionally contain ordinary imports and expands
    }
  }
}

expand SigilModuleIndex {
  logic {
    DirectoryImportSurface {
      Resolve each direct import in ModuleIndexFile using ordinary import rules.

      Build the directory-import surface from local component declarations and successfully resolved directly imported names.

      Preserve each resolved component's original declaration file and collected expansions.

      Resolve a named directory import against the resulting surface.
    }
  }

  constraints {
    ModuleIndexFile {
      ModuleIndexFile defines directory-import shorthand only.

      ModuleIndexFile does not define a workspace root, workspace member, or special component type.
    }

    ComponentVisibility {
      ModuleIndexFile does not grant or restrict component visibility.

      A component omitted from ModuleIndexFile remains importable through its explicit source path.

      Sigil defines no export or re-export form.
    }

    DirectoryImportSurface {
      Components used only as dependencies of indexed files are not added to the surface implicitly.

      Files and components elsewhere in the directory or subtree are not added implicitly.

      An explicit chain of module-index imports may make a component resolvable through multiple directory indexes.
    }

    ModuleIndexContents {
      Every ModuleIndexFile contains at least one local component declaration.
    }
  }

  cases {
    DirectoryImportSurface {
      @auth import { Session } resolves when auth/#module.sigil declares Session or directly imports Session from another Sigil source.

      @auth import { Session } is unresolved when auth/#module.sigil does not name Session, while @auth/session.sigil import { Session } remains valid.

      @auth import { Store } is unresolved when Store is only a dependency of an indexed component.

      A directory without ModuleIndexFile produces SIGIL_UNRESOLVED_IMPORT_PATH.

      A cyclic dependency involving ModuleIndexFile produces SIGIL_IMPORT_CYCLE and retains partial resolution when practical.
    }

    ModuleIndexContents {
      An imports-only ModuleIndexFile produces SIGIL_MODULE_WITHOUT_COMPONENT.
    }
  }
}
